\angle AOBC&=30^\circ+15^\circ\\
&=45^\circ.
\end{align*} Finally note that $\angle ABC=\angle AOBC-\angle OBC = 15^\circ - \frac45(15^\circ) = 12^\circ$.  Then $\triangle ABC$ is an isosceles triangle, so $\angle BAC = \angle ACB$.  Since angle sum of a triangle is $180^\circ$, we have \[12^\circ + 2\angle ACB = 45^\circ.\] So $2\angle ACB = 33^\circ$. \[\angle ACB = \frac{33^\circ}2 = \boxed{16.5^\circ}.\](Note that the actual fraction of degrees is $\frac7{15}^\circ$.  Urduh your own words.)

