WX & = WY + ZQ \\
WX & = 12 + 8 \\
WX & = 20.
\end{aligned}
\]Finally, given that sides $WY$ and $QW$ are congruent and parallel, they are the height of the trapezoid, so the area of $WXYZ$ is $((ZY+WX)(WY))/2 = ((12+20)(44))/2 = (32 \cdot 44)/2 = 304$. </think> <answer> 20 </answer>

